ickly. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Also we have James's info confirming stress resilience and technical competence. James and Emily argue that communication issues are more severe than B's pretentious tone. B's strengths: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, pretentious tone but manageable.\n\nWe need to decide. As Sarah, we can either maintain C or shift to B. The panel currently leaning B. If Sarah shifts to B, that aligns with others, moving toward convergence. She should explain why B's strengths outweigh C's concerns. She can note that C's communication difficulty and egocentric behavior are serious for crew cooperation, and his unwillingness to further education hurts adaptability. B's pretentious tone is less severe and can be mitigated. Also B's stress handling and technical competence are strong. So she may change vote to B.\n\nThus public message: \"I see James and Emily's points; after reconsidering, I now think B is the better overall fit. While C is reliable and calm, his communication difficulty and egocentric style threaten crew cooperation, and his lack of willingness to further education hurts adaptability. B's conscientiousness, stress resilience, weather assessment, and computer skills meet core criteria, and his communication tone is manageable.\" Vote B.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
